1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,510
Every year, a wall of wildebeest

2
00:00:02,510 --> 00:00:04,273
hurls itself into a river

3
00:00:04,273 --> 00:00:06,044
full of crocodiles.

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,777
Why would any animal take that risk?

5
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,426
The answer is grass.

6
00:00:11,426 --> 00:00:13,480
Rain falls at different times

7
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:16,355
across the plains, and fresh shoots follow,

8
00:00:16,355 --> 00:00:18,759
rich in protein and minerals.

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:21,611
So the herds follow the rain,

10
00:00:21,611 --> 00:00:24,435
in a clockwise loop of about 800 km

11
00:00:24,435 --> 00:00:27,058
between Tanzania and Kenya.

12
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,951
It begins in the south.

13
00:00:28,951 --> 00:00:31,398
Early in the year, up to 8,000 calves

14
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:33,333
can be born in a single day,

15
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:35,732
and they stand within minutes.

16
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,003
As the plains dry out,

17
00:00:38,003 --> 00:00:40,437
zebra and gazelle march with them,

18
00:00:40,437 --> 00:00:42,019
west and then north,

19
00:00:42,019 --> 00:00:44,331
until they reach the Mara River,

20
00:00:44,331 --> 00:00:47,175
the only reliable dry-season water.

21
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,116
From around July, they cross.

22
00:00:51,116 --> 00:00:52,869
Thousands jump at once,

23
00:00:52,869 --> 00:00:55,153
and crocodiles wait below.

24
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,528
Around 6,000 drown in an average year.

25
00:00:58,528 --> 00:01:00,265
But nothing is wasted.

26
00:01:00,265 --> 00:01:03,467
Their bones feed the river for ~7 years.

27
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,001
For decades the herd was put

28
00:01:07,001 --> 00:01:08,669
at 1.3 million.

29
00:01:08,669 --> 00:01:12,005
In 2025, an AI count from satellites

30
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:14,817
found fewer than 600,000.

31
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:17,667
Fences, farms and a shrinking river

32
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:19,691
now press on the route.

33
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,424
Keep the land open and the water flowing,

34
00:01:23,424 --> 00:01:25,951
and the great loop keeps turning.
